  "foaf:name": "Southern Ocean Microbiome and Geochemistry",
  "sdo:name": "Southern Ocean Microbiome and Geochemistry",
  "sdo:description": "Southern Ocean is one of the most important sinks of CO2 on Earth, functioning through both the biological and dissolved carbon pumps, and influence global climate and carbon cycle. As the largest upwelling system on Earth, it also serves as an essential role controlling the Earth&#x27;s global biological and elemental cycles through Antarctic Circumpolar Current (ACC). Environmental factors and the interaction of bacteria and algae affect the change and succession of phytoplankton community, and biological carbon pumping process in the SO. SOMG focus on microbial life and metabolism, carbon dynamics, trace element cycles, and historical climate changes. Under global efforts, capacity-building, and inclusive co-design and collaboration, SOMG is dedicated to developing research platforms and tools, and eco-environmental indices to understand the role of the Southern Ocean on the global carbon cycle and climate.",
  "sdo:location": "China",
  "sdo:identifier": "43.9",
